<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (The CAD Designing Internship 2026 at Nexonix Reflexo Pvt. Ltd. was designed to take a beginner from the first sketch on a workplane to a fully constrained assembly and a production-style drawing. The overall aim was to be able to model real, manufacturable components, to assemble them logically, and to communicate the design through standard documentation. This chapter explains the objectives that were achieved, with examples from the assignments completed.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
351 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 179 0 R
/T (1.1 Technical Skills)
/E (1.1 Technical Skills)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
352 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 179 0 R
/E (Every lecture was paired with a hands-on assignment, so each concept was applied immediately. Practical learning came from following a defined sequence of operations, observing the FeatureManager design tree grow feature by feature, and correcting errors when a feature failed or a sketch was under-defined. The requirement that screenshots show the full FeatureManager tree together with the model taught me to treat the tree as a record of design intent rather than as a by-product of modelling. Exporting the work as .SLDPRT, .SLDASM, .SLDDRW, .STL or .STEP files also showed how CAD data moves between design, manufacturing and other software.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
353 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 179 0 R
/T (Chapter 1: Internship Objectives)
/E (Chapter 1: Internship Objectives)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
354 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 179 0 R
/T (1.2 Practical Learning)
/E (1.2 Practical Learning)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [15]
>>
endobj
