/P 180 0 R
/E (7)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Although every assignment was individual work, the internship encouraged collaboration on ideas. Doubts were discussed with the instructor and with fellow interns, approaches to features such as Flex trim planes or the circular sketch pattern were compared, and the final deliverables were shared in a way that others could review: source files and screenshots were published to a public GitHub repository and the screenshots were posted on LinkedIn, with the links submitted through the internship portal. This workflow resembles the way design teams share and review data in industry, and it taught me to organise files and name them clearly so that others can follow the work.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
357 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 180 0 R
/T (1.4 Problem Solving)
/E (1.4 Problem Solving)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
358 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 180 0 R
/E (Several tasks required analytical thinking rather than simple repetition. Examples include deciding which plane to use as the mirror plane so that both bolt holes of the bracket remained symmetric; choosing the correct trim-plane distances and triad location so that the Flex feature bent the plate through 90 degrees; trimming the offset triangle correctly before extruding the phone stand's back support with a 24 degree draft; and determining which mate types would let the wheel spin on its shaft while the supports and bushes stayed positioned. In each case the approach was to isolate the problem, test one change at a time, and use the error messages and the status bar \(for example Under Defined\) as feedback.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
359 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 180 0 R
/T (1.3 Team Collaboration)
/E (1.3 Team Collaboration)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
