>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (The internship developed working skill in parametric CAD: sketching with constraints, creating extruded and revolved solids, applying mirror, flex, rib, draft, shell, fillet and chamfer, assembling components with mates, and creating dimensioned drawings. I also learned to read a drawing and reproduce a part from it, as in the Assignment 3 assembly, where the drawing was the specification. An important technical habit was keeping the design tree clean and logical.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
686 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 197 0 R
/T (6.2 Soft Skills)
/E (6.2 Soft Skills)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
687 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Soft skills included time management, since each assignment had a strict due date and late submissions were not accepted; attention to detail, since a small dimensional error affects later features; and self-discipline in following specifications. Working from written assignment briefs also improved my ability to interpret instructions and ask precise questions.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
688 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 197 0 R
/T (6.3 Communication)
/E (6.3 Communication)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Communication skills improved through presenting work visually. Screenshots had to show the full tree and model, GitHub repositories had to be organised, and LinkedIn posts had to describe the work clearly. Writing this report improved my technical writing, including the use of captions, tables and references.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 197 0 R
/T (6.4 Leadership)
/E (6.4 Leadership)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 197 0 R
/E (Leadership during the internship took the form of ownership. I planned the sequence of each assignment, set my own milestones before the due dates, took responsibility for the quality of my submissions, and helped peers by discussing approaches without sharing files, in line with the academic-integrity rule. This is the foundation of leading a design task in a team.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
