705 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (The internship gave exposure to industrial practice in several ways: parts designed with manufacturability in mind \(draft angles, shelling, fillets\), assembly practices \(fixed base component, mates\), standard drawing sheets \(A3 with a title block\), neutral file formats \(.STEP and .STL\) and the use of version control and professional networking platforms. It also showed that a design is complete only when it is documented well enough for someone else to build it.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
706 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (The CAD Designing Internship 2026 at Nexonix Reflexo Pvt. Ltd. gave a complete, progressive introduction to computer-aided design. Starting with simple dimensioned profiles in Week 1, the work grew to a symmetrical mounting bracket and a thin-walled phone stand in Week 2, and then to a seven-component Belt-Support Roller Unit with a full engineering drawing in Week 3. Week 4 consolidated all of this into a documented portfolio and this report.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
707 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 198 0 R
/E (The Belt-Support Roller Unit demonstrated how individual parts, each modelled with an appropriate set of features, can be assembled with mates around a fixed base component and then communicated through a drawing. The verification checks showed clean feature trees and a logically mated assembly, while also identifying clear next steps: materials, motion study, tolerancing, analysis and a surface-modelled handle.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
