<<
/Title (Assembly. The base plate was set as the fixed component, shown with the \(f\) prefix in the tree. The remaining components, namely the supports, the bushes, the shaft and the wheel, were added and positioned with mates, which are listed in the Mates folder of the assembly tree. Two copies of the support \(AM3D\) and two copies of the bush \(AM3B\) were used, because the wheel is carried on both sides.)
/Dest [23 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1773 0 R
/Next 1791 0 R
>>
endobj
1783 0 obj
<<
/Title (Activities. Every part, assembly and drawing was reopened and rebuilt to confirm that there were no rebuild errors. Sketches were checked for their Fully Defined status. The files were exported in the required formats \(.SLDPRT, .SLDASM, .SLDDRW, .STL or .STEP\), organised by assignment, and published with their screenshots. This report \(Assignment 4\) was then prepared following the Nexonix Reflexo internship report template: front matter, seven chapters, references and the formatting guidelines. Skills learned and outcome. The week improved my skills in technical documentation, version control and file organisation. The outcome was a complete, reviewable record of the internship and this report.)
/Dest [25 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1791 0 R
/Next 1774 0 R
>>
endobj
